  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental lines from governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p6); business-type from proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position Total Enterprise Funds column (p10; internal service fund excluded). Business-type receipts = operating revenues + investment earnings; interest expense, net shown as a disbursement (nonoperating net total 909,708 = 1,786,188 - 876,480); business-type net position beginning is as printed before restatement, restatement -276,433 recorded as adjustment. SBITA proceeds 10,031 placed in debt_proceeds. ending_cash is cash and cash equivalents only (p4); cash at county treasurer 510,105 and investments 17,025,046 shown separately on the balance sheet (ending_investments). Balance sheet uses government-wide total column (p1); compensated absences after one year and deferred inflows related to leases categorized as other liabilities. Budget-basis schedules (pp13-16) differ from GAAP actuals; General, Streets/Engineering, Sales Tax and 1/2 Sales Tax funds recorded from budget-and-actual schedules (Sales Tax fund page prints no expenditures; its transfers shown as net). Nonmajor combining statement has 12 funds (pp17-19) so the Total Other Governmental column (p19) is used as Nonmajor funds (combined). Transfers net on budget schedules are shown as one printed line. Read pages 1-19 of 19",
